{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FMapStructuralPaths","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapStructuralPaths","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MarkovZToCkMapping"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FMapCyclotomicDirect.is_cyclotomic_reconstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapCyclotomicDirect.is_cyclotomic_reconstruction","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapStructuralPaths.lean#L65-L65","doc":"`@marker` — opaque tag for Pathway 3 (the direct cyclotomic\nreconstruction / polynomial-matching algorithm `a_m → c_k`).\nGenuinely-open: the algorithm is not yet constructed, so this is a\ntracked opaque placeholder, not a fabricated content-bearing claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FMapCyclotomicDirect.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapCyclotomicDirect.mk","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapStructuralPaths.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FMapCyclotomicDirect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapCyclotomicDirect","kind":"class","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapStructuralPaths.lean#L53-L65","doc":"**Pathway 3: Direct Cyclotomic Reconstruction** (Option C)\n\nThe f-map acts directly on the integer Habiro coefficients $a_m \\in \\mathbb{Z}[u]$ \nto produce the $c_k$ coefficients by matching the $(q;q)_m$ poles with the \n$(1+c_k u^k)$ ladder expansion.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FMapHexagonCharacter.is_hexagon_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapHexagonCharacter.is_hexagon_derived","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapStructuralPaths.lean#L51-L51","doc":"`@marker` — opaque tag for Pathway 2 (the Hexagon-eigenvalue\nprojection extracting `c_k` from the `V_{(2,1)}` braiding eigenvalues).\nGenuinely-open: the projection is not yet constructed, so this is a\ntracked opaque placeholder, not a fabricated content-bearing claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FMapHexagonCharacter.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapHexagonCharacter.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapStructuralPaths.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FMapHexagonCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapHexagonCharacter","kind":"class","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapStructuralPaths.lean#L39-L51","doc":"**Pathway 2: Hexagon Character Extraction** (Option B)\n\nThe f-map extracts the $c_k$ ladder directly from the $V_{(2,1)}$ character difference.\nBecause $\\chi_{(2,1)} = -\\frac{(q^4+1)(q^2-1)}{4q^3}$, the Hexagon equations \nfunctorially project the eigenphase expansion onto the precision ladder.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FMapFaddeevModular.is_modular_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapFaddeevModular.is_modular_dual","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapStructuralPaths.lean#L37-L37","doc":"`@marker` — opaque tag for Pathway 1 (the explicit `Φ_q` operator\nfunctor / modular-dual transformation `q ↔ q̃`). Genuinely-open: the\nconstruction is not yet in place, so this is a tracked opaque\nplaceholder, not a fabricated content-bearing claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FMapFaddeevModular.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapFaddeevModular.mk","kind":"ctor","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapStructuralPaths.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FMapFaddeevModular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapFaddeevModular","kind":"class","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapStructuralPaths.lean#L25-L37","doc":"**Pathway 1: Faddeev Modular Dilogarithm** (Option A)\n\nThe f-map is constructed via the quantum dilogarithm $\\Phi_q$.\nThis axiomatises that `qBetaFMap` is induced by the modular dual mapping \n$q \\leftrightarrow \\tilde{q}$ on the Teichmüller space representation of the Markov trace.\n","signatureChunk":0}]}